      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A loud knocking sound and lukewarm water from your electric water heater could be due to a few reasons, but a common culprit is a sediment buildup in the tank, which can cause the tank to lose its heat retention ability. It's a good idea to have a professional inspect it, but in the meantime, you can try flushing the tank to remove any sediment. Just remember, if you're not comfortable doing it yourself, it's best to call a professional. In the meantime, you might want to consider a backup plan, like a portable water heater, just in case your main one decides to take a nap. And don't forget to keep an eye out for any signs of a leak, as that could be a sign of a more serious problem. If you do notice a leak, it's important to act quickly to prevent any further damage. And if you're ever in doubt, it's always best to consult with a professional. After all, you wouldn't want to risk a full-blown water heater apocalypse, would you?",
